From the user input, and using the guide below, you will implement server-side
authentication features using Better Auth.

# Hands on guide

This project uses [Better Auth](https://www.better-auth.com/) for
authentication. For client-side patterns, see [Auth
Client](mdc:.cursor/rules/auth-client.mdc).

## Architecture Overview

```
server/
├── lib/auth.ts           → Better Auth server config
├── api/auth/[...all].ts  → Auth API catch-all handler
├── lib/trpc.ts           → protectedProcedure middleware
└── db/auth.ts            → Auth-related DB schema
```

## Protecting tRPC Procedures

Use `protectedProcedure` instead of `baseProcedure` for routes that require
authentication. The `ctx.session` is guaranteed to be non-null in protected
procedures.

```ts
import {
  createTRPCRouter,
  protectedProcedure,
  baseProcedure,
} from "../lib/trpc";
import * as z from "zod";

export const itemsRouter = createTRPCRouter({
  // Public route - anyone can access
  public: baseProcedure.query(({ ctx }) => {
    // ctx.session might be null
    return { message: "Hello, world!" };
  }),

  // Protected route - requires authentication
  list: protectedProcedure.query(({ ctx }) => {
    // ctx.session is guaranteed to exist (TRPCContextProtected)
    const userId = ctx.session.user.id;
    return ctx.db.query.items.findMany({
      where: (items, { eq }) => eq(items.userId, userId),
    });
  }),

  // Protected mutation with input validation
  create: protectedProcedure
    .input(z.object({ name: z.string().min(1) }))
    .mutation(({ input, ctx }) => {
      return ctx.db.insert(items).values({
        id: crypto.randomUUID(),
        name: input.name,
        userId: ctx.session.user.id,
      });
    }),
});
```

## Server-side Auth Context

In tRPC procedures, auth context is available via `ctx`:

```ts
protectedProcedure.query(({ ctx }) => {
  // User info
  ctx.session.user.id;
  ctx.session.user.email;
  ctx.session.user.name;

  // Session info
  ctx.session.session.id;
  ctx.session.session.activeOrganizationId;

  // Auth API (for server-side operations)
  ctx.auth.api.getSession({ headers: ctx.event.headers });
  ctx.auth.api.verifyApiKey({ body: { key } });
});
```

## API Key Authentication (H3 Endpoints)

For external API endpoints (non-tRPC), use API key authentication:

```ts
// server/api/protected/my-endpoint.ts
import { serverAuth } from "~~/server/lib/auth";

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const auth = serverAuth(event);

  // Get API key from header
  const apiKey = getHeader(event, "x-api-key");

  if (!apiKey) {
    throw createError({
      status: 401,
      message: "Missing API key. Provide x-api-key header.",
    });
  }

  // Verify the API key
  const result = await auth.api.verifyApiKey({ body: { key: apiKey } });

  if (!result.valid) {
    throw createError({ status: 401, message: "Unauthorized" });
  }

  // Proceed with authenticated logic
  return { message: "Success!" };
});
```

## Session-based Auth in H3 Endpoints

For session-based authentication in non-tRPC endpoints:

```ts
// server/api/protected/session-endpoint.ts
import { serverAuth } from "~~/server/lib/auth";

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const auth = serverAuth(event);

  // Get session from cookies/headers
  const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers: event.headers });

  if (!session?.user) {
    throw createError({ status: 401, message: "Unauthorized" });
  }

  // Proceed with authenticated logic
  return {
    message: "Hello!",
    userId: session.user.id,
  };
});
```

## Database Schema

Auth-related tables are defined in `server/db/auth.ts`:

| Table          | Description                      |
| -------------- | -------------------------------- |
| `user`         | User accounts                    |
| `session`      | Active sessions                  |
| `account`      | OAuth/credential accounts        |
| `verification` | Email verification tokens        |
| `apikey`       | API keys for programmatic access |
| `organization` | Organizations for multi-tenancy  |
| `member`       | Organization members             |
| `invitation`   | Pending organization invitations |
| `subscription` | Stripe subscriptions             |

## TRPCContext Types

```ts
// Available in baseProcedure - session may be null
type TRPCContext = {
  event: H3Event;
  db: DrizzleDB;
  storage: StorageInterface;
  vector: VectorInterface;
  queue: QueueInterface;
  auth: BetterAuth;
  session: Session | null;
};

// Available in protectedProcedure - session is guaranteed
type TRPCContextProtected = TRPCContext & {
  session: Session; // non-null
};
```

## Server Auth Configuration

The auth server is configured in `server/lib/auth.ts` with these plugins:

- **emailAndPassword**: Email/password authentication
- **magicLink**: Passwordless email authentication
- **apiKey**: API key generation and verification
- **organization**: Multi-tenancy with roles and invitations
- **stripe**: Subscription management

```ts
// Accessing the auth instance in any H3 handler
import { serverAuth } from "~~/server/lib/auth";

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const auth = serverAuth(event);

